{"4099740": {"success": true, "data": {"type": "game", "name": "ECHO OF HUMANITY", "steam_appid": 4099740, "required_age": 0, "is_free": false, "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Echo of Humanity is an atmospheric horror experience about silence, memory, and the remnants of what was once called life.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You wake up in a place that feels familiar, yet impossibly distant.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The corridors stretch endlessly. Lights hum softly. Machines still work, though no one is left to command them.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >There are no enemies to fight. No puzzles to solve.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Only the unsettling calm of a world that has moved on - and the faint echo of something deeply human, still resonating in the void.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Echo of Humanity is less about survival, and more about understanding.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >As you explore, the environment itself begins to tell its story, through architecture, through sound, through absence.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A quiet descent into the spaces between existence and oblivion.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>FEATURES</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >🪐 Deeply immersive atmosphere of isolation and decay</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >🔊 Realistic sound design that changes with each environment</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >🚪 Liminal architecture evoking unease and nostalgia</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >📓 Narrative told through space, not exposition</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >💀 A slow, reflective horror experience with no jump scares</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Echo of Humanity invites you to wander, to listen, and to feel.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Not everything that’s gone is truly silent.</p>", "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Echo of Humanity is an atmospheric horror experience about silence, memory, and the remnants of what was once called life.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You wake up in a place that feels familiar, yet impossibly distant.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The corridors stretch endlessly. Lights hum softly. Machines still work, though no one is left to command them.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >There are no enemies to fight. No puzzles to solve.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Only the unsettling calm of a world that has moved on - and the faint echo of something deeply human, still resonating in the void.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Echo of Humanity is less about survival, and more about understanding.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >As you explore, the environment itself begins to tell its story, through architecture, through sound, through absence.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A quiet descent into the spaces between existence and oblivion.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>FEATURES</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >🪐 Deeply immersive atmosphere of isolation and decay</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >🔊 Realistic sound design that changes with each environment</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >🚪 Liminal architecture evoking unease and nostalgia</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >📓 Narrative told through space, not exposition</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >💀 A slow, reflective horror experience with no jump scares</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Echo of Humanity invites you to wander, to listen, and to feel.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Not everything that’s gone is truly silent.</p>", "short_description": "A slow, atmospheric horror experience set aboard an abandoned orbital station - the last echo of humanity. Explore cold corridors, flickering terminals, and forgotten logs of a failed salvation program. No monsters. No jumpscares. Only silence, loneliness, and the weight of extinction.", "supported_languages": "English<strong>*</strong><br><strong>*</strong>languages with full audio support", "header_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4099740/52179d3c49b5edfe58336199a9f6de948c6346f7/header.jpg?